---
// /mesonet/ag_tools/soil_profile/: soil profile plots, at the old path.
// Source: mco-website/_pages/mesonet/tools/mesonet_tools_soil_profile.md.
// Text unchanged; the figure (assets/images/soil_profile.png) is a lossless
// WebP without metadata, with written alt text.
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../../../lib/paths';
import { DASHBOARD } from '../../../lib/tools';
---
<Base short="Soil profile plots"
      description="How to read the Station Dashboard's soil profile plots: soil moisture, temperature, conductivity and water potential by depth through time.">
  <!-- Copy drafted with AI assistance; needs MCO staff review before launch (UM AI disclosure). -->
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Soil profile plots</h1>
    <p>
      The soil profile plots available on the dashboard show soil moisture (VWC), temperature,
      electrical conductivity, and soil water potential as a function of depth. For example, in the
      plot below, VWC for all of 2023 is plotted at the Bozeman HydroMet station. The bluer colors
      represent wetter conditions, while the browner colors represent drier conditions. The figure
      shows that as winter snowpack starts to melt, VWC increases, reaching as far as 20 inches
      beneath the surface. As summer begins, the three soil layers begin to dry out. Uncolored cells
      represent periods of time when the soil is frozen.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img src={url('images/mesonet/soil-profile.webp')} width="1628" height="500" loading="lazy"
           alt="Heat map of soil volumetric water content at 4, 8 and 20 inches deep at the Bozeman HydroMet station, January to December 2023, on a scale from about 12% (brown) to 37% (blue-green). All three depths are dry until April, turn wet from mid-April into July, and dry again from August through December. The 4 inch row has blank stretches in February, March and December, and the 8 inch row in December, where the soil was frozen.">
      <figcaption>Soil profile plot of volumetric water content at the Bozeman HydroMet station.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p class="method-note">
      Part of the <a href={url('mesonet/ag_tools/')}>agricultural tools</a>.
      The <a href={`${DASHBOARD}#charts`}>Station Dashboard</a> draws these plots for each station
      under Charts, Ag tools.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
